Offline TurtleBot3 Burger Webots model

TurtleBot3Burger.proto is an independently written native Webots model,
distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. It uses no external
PROTOs or online assets. Its wheel dimensions and sensor transforms follow
the local TurtleBot3 Burger robot description. Collision shapes, the fixed
low-friction caster sphere, and mass distribution are approximations.

The files in meshes/ are unmodified copies of the four meshes in
robot_description/meshes. They are derived from ROBOTIS-GIT/turtlebot3,
turtlebot3_description version 2.3.6, distributed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. See LICENSE for the full license.

Upstream: https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/turtlebot3
Installed source: /opt/ros/jazzy/share/turtlebot3_description
Upstream authors: Darby Lim, Pyo, Will Son (ROBOTIS).

The model uses a fixed, full-circle, one-layer native Webots Lidar. Its
complete ideal 360-point scan is sampled at the ROS driver update rate;
individual rays have no rotating-head acquisition delay. Noise is disabled.
The native sensor axes are x forward, y left, and z up.
